<section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl space-y-5">
  <p>
    Almost nobody was ever shown how to read a pay stub. It arrives with
    eight abbreviations on it, the number at the bottom is smaller than the
    number at the top, and the difference is simply accepted as one of the
    facts of adult life.
  </p>
  <p>
    It's also where quiet errors live for years, and where the case for
    being paid more either exists in writing or doesn't.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-14">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">Reading what you're paid</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Every line explained") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        What each deduction actually is and funds, what pre-tax versus
        after-tax means for you, and exactly how the top number became the
        bottom one.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "The arithmetic checked") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Done by the app rather than by a model, because arithmetic is not a
        thing to guess at. If it doesn't add up, you'll be told it doesn't
        add up.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "What changed since last time") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Compared against your previous stub. A deduction that appeared, a
        rate that moved, hours that came out wrong — the things that
        otherwise go unnoticed for a year.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "If they didn't pay you") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Missing hours, unpaid overtime, a final paycheck that never arrived
        — a formal demand, which is a real and effective step that most
        people don't know is available to them.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-14">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">Asking for more</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Built from what you logged") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Two years of small recorded wins become a memo you could actually
        send. This is why logging them takes ten seconds at the time — the
        payoff is a document you'd otherwise have to reconstruct from
        nothing.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "A script, and a walkaway") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Talking points, an opening, what to say when they say no, and — the
        part people skip — deciding your walkaway before you're in the room
        rather than during.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">It won't invent the market rate</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    A number a model made up about what your role pays is worse than no
    number, because you'd walk in and say it. Where a fact has to come from
    outside, the app tells you which fact to go and get, and helps you use
    it once you have it.
  </p>
</section>
